# Cursor Project Rules for MDKV

## Principles
- Favor test-driven, modular design. Keep orchestrators thin; put logic in modules.
- Docs should be concise, demonstrative, and kept in sync with code (docstrings + Sphinx).
- Prefer real data paths in examples; avoid mocks in documented flows.

## Code Style
- Python 3.9+; explicit, readable names (no 1–2 char vars).
- Guard clauses over deep nesting; handle errors/edges early.
- Keep comments minimal; document "why".
- Public API documented via docstrings; update `docs/api.rst` if surfacing new modules.
- Use `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` — never `datetime.utcnow()` (deprecated in 3.12+).

## Package Structure
- `mdkv.core`: data model + validation
- `mdkv.storage`: persist/load `.mdkv` (ZIP + YAML manifest), `MDKVFormatError`
- `mdkv.services`: search/export utilities
- `mdkv.cli`: CLI entrypoints (`python -m mdkv` also works via `__main__.py`)
- `mdkv.gui`: FastAPI web GUI
- `mdkv.common`: logging utilities
- `mdkv.library`: example definition builder
- `mdkv.demo`: demo document builder

## Track Types
`primary`, `translation`, `commentary`, `code`, `reference`, `media_ref`, `revision`.

## Model API
- `Track.to_dict()` / `Track.from_dict()` — JSON serialization
- `MDKVDocument.to_dict()` / `MDKVDocument.from_dict()` — JSON serialization
- `MDKVDocument.count_tracks_by_type()` — type→count mapping
- `__repr__` on both `Track` and `MDKVDocument`

## Validation
- ERROR: missing title, authors, primary track; duplicate track paths.
- WARN: empty content, code tracks without fences, translation without language,
  bad version format, multiple primary tracks.
- `ValidationIssue` carries `track_id` for track-level issues.

## Search
- `search_document()` supports `case_insensitive=True` flag
- `SearchMatch` includes `track_type` and `language`

## Export
- `to_markdown()` supports `metadata_header=True` for YAML frontmatter
- `to_html()` supports `include_track_types` and `metadata_header`
- `export_to_files()` returns `List[Path]` of written files

## Documentation
- Pages: concept, format, architecture, usage, CLI, API, license.
- Build: `uv run sphinx-build -b html docs docs/_build/html`.
- Keep README pointers: concept, format, architecture, CLI, examples.

## Public API
- Re-exported in `mdkv/__init__.py`: `MDKVDocument`, `Track`, `allowed_track_types`,
  `ValidationError`, `validate_document`, `ValidationIssue`, `search_document`,
  `SearchMatch`, `to_markdown`, `to_html`, `export_to_files`, `save_mdkv`, `load_mdkv`,
  `MDKVFormatError`.
- If adding API, update `__all__`, docstrings, and docs.
- `py.typed` marker present for PEP 561.

## CLI Commands
`init`, `info`, `list-tracks`, `add-track`, `remove-track`, `rename-track`,
`update-track`, `export`, `export-tracks`, `search` (with `-i`), `validate`,
`set-meta`, `get-meta`, `import`, `diff`, `stats`, `gui`, `license`.

## GUI API Endpoints
- CRUD: `/api/document`, `/api/track`, `/api/tracks`, `/api/open`, `/api/save`
- Render: `/api/render/html`, `/api/render/markdown`, `/api/render/track_html`,
  `/api/render/all_html`, `/api/render/tracks_html`
- Operations: `/api/search`, `/api/stats`, `/api/diff`, `/api/validate`
- Library: `/api/library`, `/api/status`

## Examples & Definitions
- `library/definitions/` are canonical YAML samples.
- Examples: `create_doc`, `validate_doc`, `export_html`, `search_docs`, `roundtrip`,
  `logged_workflow`, `load_from_yaml`, `import_example`, `diff_example`, `stats_example`.

## CI Guidance
- Validate docs build + run tests on each change.
- Run: `uv run pytest -q --cov=mdkv --cov-report=term-missing`
- Python 3.14 in CI.
